tness. Holding the `Request` in `AsyncLocalStorage` wouldn't help after `forward` returns, because the store's scope ends about when the frame's does. A repair would add code for no case that exists.\n\n## What I also checked\n\n- The gate at 15758339 exits 0. Its `test.log` shows Node 98, Counting 56, Plain 3,206 with one skip and Native 890 with two skips. From there to this head, only the note and the manifest change.\n- The evidence verifies. All 12 manifest rows match, the directory has 44 files, its `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with digest 2ad1c819, and no file is writable.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 93a6b661 gives tree 9add2af5. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `check-commit-messages` checks 2 with 0 flagged, and `git diff --check` is clean. The worktree stayed clean.\n\nNo container, Git host or real `fetch` ran, as the note says. I ran no independent second read.\n\n## Architecture\n\nNo source changes. The note records the reachability as a limit. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nA lost abort here would leave upstream work running, and the witness shows that it doesn't during a forward. No credential path changes. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nOne case settles the question without new code. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's check holds. No deployment follows.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:88494fd5336eed0be0dcb28d280ba6c0b443ff9e","binding":"assigned","head":"4f14e0fbb9aef0c3b3940f7df837c926596e7fea","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:75b7ac52f5400b68e6dd00842420cc08d522e3cc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:48541f48af8898e3f9cdcb5d4f4bb5a26bd1d914\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:75b7ac52f5400b68e6dd00842420cc08d522e3cc","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stal